{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789238019,"nonce":"pp4YSNVmNWOTse4fT/8X1ggjP2I=","title":"Runtime seam: let a host supply the memory under the Immix strategy","message":"wren_lift keeps its Immix (gc_immix.rs) and depends on nothing. What it\ngains is a seam a host can install into before the first VM exists: a\nversioned repr(C) table of function-pointer slots for the operations the\nImmix strategy performs on memory, filled with wren_lift's own block\nallocator by default. Same pattern as ash_std::rt: an atomic slot per\nentry, an installer export (wlift_rt_install), refused once any VM has\nallocated, and wlift_rt_installed.\n\nWhat the table covers is what a replacement heap owns: raw allocation by\nsize (alloc_raw), resolving an address to its allocation start\n(containing_allocation), whether an address is a heap pointer, marking an\nallocation live for this cycle, the conservative scan of a stack range,\nexternal-pressure accounting, and the collection driver (mark from the\ngiven roots and ranges, then sweep). What stays wren_lift's whatever hosts\nit: ObjHeader and every Obj layout, mark_value / trace_object /\nprocess_gray_stack (precise marking through the object visitors),\ndrop_in_place_by_type (release of Rust-owned containers at sweep), the\nintern table, the VM's root gathering, the write-barrier flag, hatch.\n\nUnder a host the two collectors meet at two callbacks the host needs from\nwren_lift: a per-object trace (the host asks wren_lift to mark an object's\nchildren through its visitors) and a per-object drop (the host tells\nwren_lift a dead object's containers must be released before its memory\nis recycled). Both exist today as free functions; the table carries them\nback to the host as slots wren_lift fills.\n\nDefault path indistinguishable from today: one relaxed load and an\nindirect call per slot. Every existing wlift_* export keeps its name.\nSelecting GcStrategy::Immix with a host installed makes that VM's Immix\nrun on the host's memory; the other strategies are untouched.\n\nVerification: wren_lift's suite unchanged with nothing installed; a\nunit test that installs a counting table and sees it hit; and, on the\nhost's side, the same suite through a runner that installs first.","files":null}]}